    "note": "Wright 1834 draws a narrow winding watercourse running north out of the main stem, across Kinzie Street, ending at Michigan Street. Its existence and course are documented by the map; this is a CENTRELINE because the bank wash survives only in 5 fragments \u2014 the pink Kinzie ward band and the lot lines it crosses erase the rest \u2014 so a traced boundary would be a fiction. Probably one of the three sloughs off the Main Branch shown on the 1830 Thompson plat. Depth is conjectural: no source gives one.",
